COO Controls — Key Priorities

Controls Town Hall — June 30, 2026: “2026 Areas of Focus”

* Best-in-Class Risk and Control Practices: Set industry-leading practices and move beyond regulatory compliance.
* AI Enablement & Continuous Improvement: Leverage Generative AI & Agentic AI to reimagine controls, end-to-end.
* Enhanced Client and Colleague Experience: Prioritize client and colleague experience in control design and operation.
* Connectivity & Interoperability: Embed a culture of interoperability and accountability across Citi.
* AI proficient Risk & Control Workforce: AI and process proficiency as a core competency across Control Colleagues.
* “One Controls” Mindset: All Controls Teams engaged, working together to meet common goals.

Historical context — not presented as 2026 priorities

* Q1 2025 COO Controls Town Hall: Strengthening controls design, adoption, and automation; Issue Management; Automation and Reporting.
* Update on Transformation — May 2025: Standardizing and strengthening our controls to improve effectiveness and reduce risk; infrastructure modernization, platform consolidation, automation.


