U.S. Consumer Cards — Key Priorities

Business ambition: “Consistent investments will drive sustained, profitable growth and deliver strong returns through the cycle.”

* Growth and acquisition: Refresh and launch new products; Upgrade acquisitions & scale marketing.
* Risk and underwriting: Risk modernization; Enhance Underwriting; Proactively Manage Fraud, Credit Abuse, and Scams.
* Data and decisioning: Data availability and usability for business decisioning; Work with Partners to build shared data lakes to improve decisioning.
* Digital experience and servicing: Build best-in-class digital experience; Modernize customer servicing capabilities.
* Technology and efficiency: Modernize to real-time, intelligent platforms; Boost PDLC agility by rationalizing software & AI costs.
* AI adoption and delivery: Rapidly embed AI across the business; Scale AI PDLC pilot across USCC.
* Partners and commerce: Elevate Partner Card growth and returns; Enhance Lifestyle Platform; Launch Commerce Media.

Selected priorities from the supplied 1Q26, 2Q26 EAW and July 21, 2026 Technology Town Hall slides.
